{% doc %}
Renders a section's closing call-to-action row.

Most won sections were pure content: a comparison table, a stats band, a USP
strip all made the case and then left the shopper with nowhere to go. This is the
shared "and now buy" row — one markup, one set of setting ids, so a merchant
learns it once and every section behaves the same.

Renders NOTHING unless both a label and a link are set, so a section that has not
been given a CTA stays exactly as it was (theme-block-ux rule 5: never a broken
empty button).

@param {object} cfg - the section's settings (pass `s`). NOT named `settings`:
  that is Liquid's GLOBAL theme-settings object, and a parameter of the same name
  does not shadow it — every lookup silently resolved against theme settings, the
  keys were always blank, and the CTA never rendered anywhere.
@param {string} [align] - 'start' | 'center' | 'end'; defaults to the section's content_align
@example
{% render 'won-section-cta', cfg: s %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  # `break` outside a for loop is not a guard — it is undefined behaviour in
  # Liquid. Gate the markup with a plain if instead.
  assign cta_label = cfg.cta_button_label
  assign cta_link = cfg.cta_button_link
  assign cta_align = align | default: cfg.content_align | default: 'center'
  assign cta_flex = 'center'
  if cta_align == 'left' or cta_align == 'start'
    assign cta_flex = 'flex-start'
  elsif cta_align == 'right' or cta_align == 'end'
    assign cta_flex = 'flex-end'
  endif
-%}
{%- if cta_label != blank and cta_link != blank -%}
<div class="won-section-cta" style="--won-cta-justify: {{ cta_flex }};">
  {% render 'won-button',
    label: cta_label,
    link: cta_link,
    style: cfg.cta_button_style,
    new_tab: cfg.cta_button_new_tab,
    class: 'won-section-cta__btn'
  %}
  {%- if cfg.cta_note != blank -%}
    <p class="won-section-cta__note">{{ cfg.cta_note }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
